# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# Restructured 2026-08-27 (see docs/idealization_report.md, 2026-08-26 and
# 2026-08-27 sprints). The Vite build emits dist/index.html (the public
# marketing landing page, physically at the build root) and dist/app.html
# (the operational 3D canvas app — requires a LAN-local backend, never
# meant to be what a public domain root serves).
#
# No rule needed here, deliberately — confirmed empirically, not assumed:
#   - "/"        -> served directly from the literal root index.html, 200,
#                   no redirect.
#   - "/app"     -> Cloudflare Pages' default clean-URL asset resolution
#                   serves app.html's content directly, 200, no redirect
#                   or rule required.
#   - "/app.html"/"/index.html" (direct .html requests) -> Cloudflare's
#                   built-in HTML canonicalization 308s these to /app and
#                   / respectively. Harmless, single-hop.
#
# An earlier version of this file had an explicit `/app /app.html 200`
# rewrite rule, reasoning it would give /app a clean URL. It didn't —
# routing that request through the rewrite engine made Cloudflare's
# canonicalizer redirect /app to /app (itself), an infinite loop (curl
# --max-redirs confirmed it, both locally via `wrangler pages dev dist`
# and live). Reproduced, root-caused, and reverted in the same sprint
# that introduced it; see the 2026-08-27 entry for the full story. Do not
# re-add a rewrite rule for /app without re-verifying against this exact
# failure mode.
